# KNOWN GAP — BOTH REAL BACKENDS, `gg check` accepts, rc 139.
#
# Evidence for todo/t0406 (non-identifier-callee / signature-erased container
# element). What this cell DISCRIMINATES from that item's existing repros:
# they all carry a `&` sigil, so their story is "the borrow tag never reaches
# either ABI channel". This one has NO sigil at all — a pure by-value
# `Callable[int(int)]` — and it dies just the same, which shows the defect is
# the element signature collapsing to the zero-parameter fallback
# `fn() -> i64`, not the sigil tagging.
#
# `push` + `len()` on the same vector is GREEN (the closure-packing wrap at
# `AbiKind::VoidElem` handles the write); only calling the element back out
# dies, on BOTH read shapes below.
#
# DISCRIMINATED from todo/t0873, the other open `Vector[Callable]` item: that
# one is a container-LITERAL SEGV and a NULL `elem_drop` (the pushed envs leak).
# This cell pushes, so it is past the literal arm, and it dies on the CALL, not
# at drop.
#
# INTENDED (asserted by the wired test): prints `1` then `42` then `42`.

void main():
    Callable[int(int)] f = (int x): x * 2
    Vector[Callable[int(int)]] fs = []
    fs.push(f.clone())
    print(f"{fs.len()}")
    # index-read call
    print(f"{fs[0](21)}")
    # get-chain call through a bound local
    Callable[int(int)] g = fs.get(0).unwrap()
    print(f"{g(21)}")
